  "review_scope": "Pinned source inspection and six hash-verified saved P83 controls. No live budget intervention or sampling test. Original private histories were not printed.",
  "findings": [
    "Output max counts every generated token across reasoning and public output; reaching it does not require a complete action.",
    "reasoning_budget_tokens has a thinking_budget_tokens alias and is passed only if the session exposes thinking end tags.",
    "MiniMax-M3 exposes thinking start/end tags. The six saved P83 controls all had budget -1 and reasoning_control false.",
    "The sampler forces an ending token sequence when the per-block budget expires. UTF-8 completion and the ending sequence can add tokens. A later thinking start can open another full budget window.",
    "Lazy grammar is suppressed during active thinking and receives the matching ending sequence on transition; grammar existence does not guarantee completion before total cap.",
    "Changing the budget can change reasoning and action selection. It cannot establish preserved task quality from static inspection."
  ]
}
